<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
    <version>3.5.16</version>
    <relativePath/>
  </parent>

  <groupId>com.edunext.edutrack</groupId>
  <artifactId>edutrack-parent</artifactId>
  <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
  <packaging>pom</packaging>
  <name>EduTrack — parent</name>
  <description>Organisation task and client ticketing platform</description>

  <modules>
    <module>common</module>
    <module>domain</module>
    <module>api</module>
    <module>worker</module>
  </modules>

  <properties>
    <java.version>25</java.version>
    <maven.compiler.release>25</maven.compiler.release>
    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>

    <mapstruct.version>1.6.3</mapstruct.version>
    <!--
      A-020: raised from 2.6.0, which is not compatible with the Spring
      Framework 6.2 that Boot 3.5.16 brings. 2.6.0 calls the
      `ControllerAdviceBean(Object)` constructor that 6.2 removed, so building
      the OpenAPI document throws NoSuchMethodError as soon as the application
      contains ANY @ControllerAdvice:

        Handler dispatch failed: java.lang.NoSuchMethodError:
          'void org.springframework.web.method.ControllerAdviceBean.<init>(java.lang.Object)'

      It was dormant only because nothing had declared one yet. It would have
      surfaced for whichever stream added the first exception handler — and as
      a 500 from /v3/api-docs, which reads as a springdoc problem rather than a
      version problem. Stream D owns the OpenAPI stack; flagged for Debashis
      rather than bumped silently.
    -->
    <springdoc.version>2.8.9</springdoc.version>
    <testcontainers.version>1.20.4</testcontainers.version>
    <shedlock.version>5.16.0</shedlock.version>
    <!--
      A-037: raised from 1.3.0, which cannot read this project's own bytecode.
      ArchUnit shades ASM, and 1.3.0's copy is 9.6 — class file major version
      65, i.e. Java 21. We compile to 25, which is major version 69.

      The failure mode is the reason this is a comment and not a one-line bump.
      ArchUnit does not throw on a class file it cannot parse: it logs and skips
      it. Every class was skipped, so the import returned an empty set, and an
      empty set satisfies every rule of the form "no class should do X" —
      instantly, with no warning, and in the build log indistinguishable from a
      clean codebase. Nine rules reported green while checking nothing.

      1.3.0 was declared here long before any rule existed and was therefore
      never exercised, which is how it sat at a version that could not read the
      project. ArchImportSanityTest now asserts the import is non-empty and
      names a class from each module, so the next time this drifts — a Java 26
      release, most likely — it fails as a missing canary rather than as
      silence.
    -->
    <archunit.version>1.4.2</archunit.version>
    <bouncycastle.version>1.79</bouncycastle.version>
    <awssdk.version>2.29.29</awssdk.version>
    <poi.version>5.3.0</poi.version>
    <!--
      A-064 · PDF export. PLAN.md §2.2 names Apache POI for Excel and names
      nothing at all for PDF, so this is a stack decision the plan did not
      carry — recorded as a new §2.2 row rather than added quietly.

      OpenPDF rather than iText: iText 5 is AGPL and iText 7 is commercially
      licensed, and neither is a licence to acquire by accident inside a
      product an organisation will sell. OpenPDF is the LGPL/MPL fork of
      iText 4, which is the last version under that licence.

      Rather than PDFBox, which is Apache 2.0 and already a sibling of POI:
      PDFBox positions text by coordinate and has no table primitive, so a
      report of any width means hand-rolling column layout, wrapping and page
      breaks. That is the whole job here, and OpenPDF's PdfPTable does it.
    -->
    <openpdf.version>2.0.3</openpdf.version>
    <!--
      C-029: the server-side half of PLAN.md §3.9. Stream C is adding a
      dependency to Stream A's build file, which the working agreement asks be
      said out loud rather than done quietly — flagged for Debashis in the PR.

      §3.9 is normative and unambiguous: sanitisation happens "on the server, on
      write, always … the only sanitiser an attacker cannot skip is the one on
      the write path". Until now only the client copy existed
      (`components/ui/rich-text.ts`), which §3.9 itself calls advice. The
      comment box is the first field written by one user and rendered to
      another, so it is where the missing half stops being theoretical.

      jsoup over OWASP's html-sanitizer because `Safelist` maps almost
      one-to-one onto §3.9's fourteen tags and two protocol rules, so
      `CommentSanitizer` reads as the spec rather than as a builder DSL around
      it. Both are maintained and either would do; this one makes the
      correspondence checkable by eye.
    -->
    <jsoup.version>1.18.3</jsoup.version>
  </properties>

  <dependencyManagement>
    <dependencies>
      <!-- internal modules -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>com.edunext.edutrack</groupId>
        <artifactId>edutrack-common</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
      </dependency>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>com.edunext.edutrack</groupId>
        <artifactId>edutrack-domain</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- mapping -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
        <artifactId>mapstruct</artifactId>
        <version>${mapstruct.version}</version>
      </dependency>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
        <artifactId>mapstruct-processor</artifactId>
        <version>${mapstruct.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- OpenAPI: Stream D owns the contract (D-001…D-005) -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
        <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
        <version>${springdoc.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- scheduler locking, so scanners don't double-fire across instances -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>net.javacrumbs.shedlock</groupId>
        <artifactId>shedlock-spring</artifactId>
        <version>${shedlock.version}</version>
      </dependency>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>net.javacrumbs.shedlock</groupId>
        <artifactId>shedlock-provider-jdbc-template</artifactId>
        <version>${shedlock.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- Argon2id (PLAN.md §10.3) -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.bouncycastle</groupId>
        <artifactId>bcprov-jdk18on</artifactId>
        <version>${bouncycastle.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- object storage -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>software.amazon.awssdk</groupId>
        <artifactId>s3</artifactId>
        <version>${awssdk.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- Excel import — POI streaming only (PLAN.md §2.2) -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.apache.poi</groupId>
        <artifactId>poi-ooxml</artifactId>
        <version>${poi.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- PDF export — A-064. See the version property for why OpenPDF. -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>com.github.librepdf</groupId>
        <artifactId>openpdf</artifactId>
        <version>${openpdf.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- Rich-text sanitisation on the write path (PLAN.md §3.9) — C-029 -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.jsoup</groupId>
        <artifactId>jsoup</artifactId>
        <version>${jsoup.version}</version>
      </dependency>

      <!-- test -->
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
        <artifactId>testcontainers-bom</artifactId>
        <version>${testcontainers.version}</version>
        <type>pom</type>
        <scope>import</scope>
      </dependency>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>com.tngtech.archunit</groupId>
        <artifactId>archunit-junit5</artifactId>
        <version>${archunit.version}</version>
        <scope>test</scope>
      </dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </dependencyManagement>

  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <pluginManagement>
      <plugins>
        <plugin>
          <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
          <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
          <configuration>
            <annotationProcessorPaths>
              <path>
                <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
                <artifactId>mapstruct-processor</artifactId>
                <version>${mapstruct.version}</version>
              </path>
            </annotationProcessorPaths>
            <compilerArgs>
              <arg>-parameters</arg>
            </compilerArgs>
          </configuration>
        </plugin>
      </plugins>
    </pluginManagement>
  </build>
</project>
